    {
      "page_title": "End-to-End Flows & Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flows End To End",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "POST /articles -> 201 Created",
            "Location: /articles/77",
            "# body = the created article"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`PUT /articles/77` with `If-Match` → 200 or 204",
            "200 when returning the entity, 204 when the client has it",
            "412 when the ETag is stale"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`DELETE /articles/77` → 204",
            "Repeat call → 404 or 410",
            "Blocked by dependents → 409"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Answer"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bad password",
              "401"
            ],
            [
              "too many attempts",
              "429 + `Retry-After`"
            ],
            [
              "malformed JSON",
              "400"
            ],
            [
              "`email: \"nope\"`",
              "422 + problem+json"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Async End To End",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "POST /reports",
              "202 + /jobs/5",
              "GET /jobs/5",
              "200 running",
              "303 to /reports/91"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 202 Accepted",
            "Location: /jobs/5",
            "# poll this, don't wait"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "202 means ==queued==, outcome not guaranteed",
            "Job resource returns 200 with its status while running",
            "On finish: **303** See Other to the result"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Ways To Get It Wrong",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "200 for everything with `success: false` — breaks monitoring and caches",
            "500 for validation errors — pages on-call for a user's typo",
            "401 when you meant 403 — clients loop re-authenticating forever",
            "302 after a POST when you meant 303 or 307 — body silently lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Ship",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assert the status code in tests, not just the body",
            "A route returning 200 instead of 201 breaks contracts silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Code First, Then Words",
          "text": "The status code is the API's protocol-level answer; the body is the human-level detail. Get the code right, then explain in `problem+json`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "403 Forbidden: The Hard No",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "403 = **Forbidden**",
            "Server **understands** the request",
            "Server **identifies** the user",
            "Server **refuses** the action"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. The Core Distinction",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Meaning",
            "Action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "401",
              "Who are you?",
              "Authenticate"
            ],
            [
              "403",
              "I know you, no.",
              "Stop"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Why Re-auth Fails",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Identity is already **verified**",
            "Permission is **denied**",
            "New token = same identity",
            "Same identity = same **denial**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Loop Trap",
          "text": "Clients that retry 403 with new tokens create an infinite loop. Detect 403 and stop immediately."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common Triggers",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "User lacks required **role**",
            "Resource belongs to **another** user",
            "IP address is **blocked**",
            "API key is **expired**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Response Body",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{\"status\": 403,",
            " \"title\": \"Forbidden\",",
            " \"detail\": \"Insufficient permissions\"}"
          ],
          "note": "Keep it vague for security"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. 403 or 404?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "403 **confirms** the resource exists",
            "404 can ==hide existence== from unauthorized callers",
            "Private resources often answer 404 to outsiders"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Scenario",
            "Code"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "no token",
              "401"
            ],
            [
              "private, not yours",
              "404"
            ],
            [
              "visible, no write",
              "403"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. 403 vs 405",
          "ink": "blue"
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Identity vs Permission"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "403 vs 405 & 401, Securely Handled",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "403 = __you__ may not delete this",
            "405 = this resource is **never** deletable",
            "405 MUST send an `Allow:` header"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "DELETE /invoices/9",
            "HTTP/1.1 405 Method Not Allowed",
            "Allow: GET, HEAD"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Preflight Gotcha",
          "text": "Never answer a CORS `OPTIONS` preflight with 401/403. Return 200 or 204 without auth, or every browser client breaks."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Security Note",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Do **not** leak specific rules",
            "Avoid revealing **which** permission failed",
            "Consistent message prevents **enumeration**",
            "Log the **reason** server-side"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Client Handling",
          "items": [
            "Show \"Access Denied\" UI",
            "Do **not** retry automatically",
            "Offer \"Request Access\" link",
            "Log the event for audit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. vs 401 Comparison",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Aspect",
            "401",
            "403"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Identity",
              "Unknown",
              "Known"
            ],
            [
              "Token",
              "Missing/Invalid",
              "Valid"
            ],
            [
              "Retry",
              "Yes",
              "No"
            ],
            [
              "Header",
              "`WWW-Authenticate`",
              "none"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Real-World Example",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "GET /admin/users",
            "Authorization: Bearer valid_token",
            "HTTP/1.1 403 Forbidden",
            "# User is valid, not admin"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "11. Login Flow",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Code"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bad password",
              "401"
            ],
            [
              "account suspended",
              "403"
            ],
            [
              "too many attempts",
              "429"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Identity vs Permission"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "403 Best Practices & Testing",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests",
            "Retry-After: 60",
            "# seconds or an HTTP-date"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "200 with `error: true` on a denied request",
            "500 when a permission check fails",
            "302 to a login page from a JSON API"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "12. Best Practices",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Return 403 for **permission** failures",
            "Return 401 for **authentication** failures",
            "Never return 200 with `error: true`",
            "Use `WWW-Authenticate` only for 401"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "13. Test It",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "r = client.get(\"/admin/users\",",
            "    headers=auth(viewer))",
            "assert r.status_code == 403"
          ],
          "note": "assert the code, not the body"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Role-less user on admin route → 403",
            "Another user's resource → 403 or 404, consistently",
            "Expired token → 401, never 403"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaway",
          "text": "403 is a final answer. The client has done everything right except having the right permissions. Stop retrying."
        }
      ],
      "subtitle": "Identity vs Permission"
    }
